  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram below shows the energy levels for a hydrogen atom and a transition made by an electron.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which of the following values is closest to the frequency of the photon emitted during this transition?</p>\n<p>(Use <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"h = 6.63 \\times 10^{-34}\"></span> J s and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1 \\text{ eV} = 1.60 \\times 10^{-19}\"></span> J)</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.6 \\times 10^{14}\"></span> Hz</p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.5 \\times 10^{15}\"></span> Hz</p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.9 \\times 10^{15}\"></span> Hz</p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3.3 \\times 10^{14}\"></span> Hz</p></li></ol>"
